title: FirstLoopBoat
---
<<declare $SecondLoopBoat = true>>
<<declare $sashaDick = false>>
<<declare $SecretWord = true>>
<<declare $DudeTheyJustSaidThat = false>>

<<if $SecondLoopBoat == true>>
	<<jump SecondLoopBoat>>
<<endif>>
The air is thicker here, damp. It may be the water that laps easily by the shoreside, but you think that the giant dark lake is likely the cause of it. 
As you pass by the pier, a sudden hiss cuts through your thoughts.
DrBoatguy phD: “Psst, hey, kid. Over here!”

It’s a wayfarer, or ferryman. You remember when you were growing up this was one of the jobs you desperately wanted to have as your own. 
It was once a specialty, a task only delegated to those most well-versed with rivers and in line with religious ideals. Now, it seems to be booming business-- and they have to fight for your attention.
That, or this particular ferryman has an eye for the dramatics.


Dr. Boatguy phD: “Just ten moneys, I’ll give you a ride from all the way point A to B."
Dr. Boatguy phD: "What are points A and B? That’s up to you- but I’m the cheapest. Don’t listen to the others. Seriously, they’ll chat your ear off. Real annoying if you ask me.”


->"Who are you?"
->"Why are you like this?"
    <<set $sashaDick = true>>


Dr. Boatguy phD: “Hm? Oh! I’m dr. Boatguy Phd. Quite the celebrity around here if you ask me- but you can ask me a lot, really.”

They spread out their arms theatrically, referring to the invisible crowd around them. Of course, there’s no one really there, but they seem to be very amused by their own joke.

->You have a doctorate?	
->Boatguy? Is that your real name?

Dr. Boatguy phD: “Allegedly.”
Their grin gets wider, if that’s even possible. They seem to be having a great time pulling your leg- though after a moment it falls when they see how utterly unamused you are.
Dr. Boatguy phD: “Anyway. So kid, since you’re not begging me to consider you for a ride in my boat, what else can I do ya for? Really, you can ask me a lot. I’m a bit of a….”


They trail off, attempting to figure out the possible name as they squint at you. It’s like they think you’re going to fill in the blanks.
Though, they don’t wait for you to.


Dr. Boatguy phD: “Tour guide! Right. Anyway, what can I do ya for?”
<<jump tree1>>


===
title: tree1
---
//Dialogue Tree 1
    ->"What’s the best place to go here?"
        <<jump bestplacetogo>>
    ->"Okay but- why are you like this?" <<if $sashaDick is true>>
        <<jump sashawhywouldyousaythat>>
    ->"I’m looking for my brother, Dmitriy."
        <<jump wheresdmitriy>>
   
===
title: bestplacetogo
---
Dr. Boatguy phD: “Well damn, kid. You’re asking me a lot just by one question. The best, the best? Solster is always the best, know that?”


They let out a long, thoughtful hum, stroking their imaginary beard before their finger jots up.


Dr. Boatguy phD: “So you’d think, right, that the best thing is the parade? Naw, naw, ‘round here, it’s the food! Good stuff, really.”


They point at you, halting all dialogue with a heavy pause.


Dr. Boatguy phD: “You look new here, and I don’t mean in the ‘you’re an outsider’ new, but like in the ‘you look like a newborn foal who’s seeing the greenest pasture of its life’ new. Is this your first time in Solster?”
You remember vaguely meeting Boat before.. They were one of your brother’s friends, you’re sure.
They don’t seem to share that remembrance, clearly.


//Dialogue Tree 2
-> I’m not new, I grew up here.
    Dr. Boatguy phD: “..Seriously? Then why are you asking me what the best place to go is?”
    <<jump tree1>>
-> Well, sort of.
    Dr. Boatguy phD: “Hell yeah! I’ve got an eye for this stuff, really. My mother always told me; Boats- she’d call me that, Boats. It’s hilarious- but she said, Boats! You’re too damn perceptive for your own good. And I’d tell her- yeah well ma! I do like lookin’ at people and figurin’ out what their mind’s all about. Riveting stuff.”
Dr. Boatguy phD: “..What did you ask again?”


Before you can open your mouth to reply, Boatguy continues talking.


Dr. Boatguy phD: “Right! Right. Where you gotta go.. You can try the local café this side of the river! It’s not nearly as good as half of the other ones otherside, but they blocked off the road ‘cos of the parade.”


Boat juts their chin in the direction of a small, dimly lit restaurant on the cornerstone of the street. 
The board over the door says Hpalr's. It’s surprisingly packed inside- and you’d need some luck to get in and get food. 
Regardless, the ferryman sniffs in disdain when they continue speaking.


Dr. Boatguy phD: “Look, I aint sayin’ it’s bad- it’s edible, really! Just folks think they’re.. Well, we’ve all got our opinions on what’s the best food, eh? Just think the train supply is always a bit too eager to give them first pick. But whatever- I’m just a ferryman, what do I know?”
They pause for just long enough that you think they're about to stop, but they continue talking right as you open your mouth.
Dr. Boatguy phD: "And the [i]owner[/i]! Pfah, it's like he's a character in and of itself. Kicked me out of his restaurant once, he did. Because I [i]talked too much[/i] he said."
Dr. Boatguy phD: "We've been mortal enemies ever since."
They're quiet now, to the point it got awkward. You clear your throat to speak again, expecting another interruption that never comes.
<<jump tree1>>

===
title: sashawhywouldyousaythat
---
Dr. Boatguy phD: “Uh,”
Boatguy looks around as if referring to their aforementioned invisible audience for moral support. Though after finding none, they stare at you blankly.
Dr. Boatguy phD: “Because it’s funny?”
Now even they sound unsure.
<<jump tree1>>


===
title: wheresdmitriy
---

Dr. Boatguy phD: “Oh! Dmi-”
Dr. Boatguy phD: “Dmi-”
Dr. Boatguy phD: “Your broth-”
Dr. Boatguy phD: “You’re–”
Dr. Boatguy phD: “Huh?”


Boatguy seems.. Genuinely startled by the information you’ve just given them. They fall uncharacteristically silent, face blank as they process this information.
Then, their face breaks out into a wide, beaming smile.


Dr. Boatguy phD: “You’re Dmitriy’s sibling, are you? Oh my goodness! He’ll be so excited to see you’re back!”

Their excitement, while a little overwhelming, is equally as infectious. For a moment you can truly and deeply believe someone’s excited to see you.
They open their mouth then close it again, visibly hesitating with their next sentence as if they’re being held back by invisible string. Then, they hesitantly speak up again.
Dr. Boatguy phD: “Has he.. He’s... Um, I think he should be near the parade, actually! He's on break now, though..”
You can tell that’s not what Boatguy [i]wanted[/i] to say, but their eyes are lighting up in a way that’s almost unbecoming. Are they hiding something?
-> Is something the matter?
	Dr. Boatguy phD: “The matter? No, no.. not at all…”
	The ferryman is horribly unsubtle, but it's clear that there’s no use trying to pry this information out of them. 
	You’ll find out sooner or later, whether you want to or not.
	-> Alright then.
	-> Great.
-> Okay.. thanks. 
They nod vehemently, giving a big wave that spans in an arc over their head.
Dr. Boatguy phD: “Say hi for me when you see him!”
With that, they turn away from you, done with the conversation even if you might not be. Every few moments they glance over their shoulder at you, eyes sparkling with excitement.
Strange man.

===
title: SecondLoopBoat
---

Dr. Boatguy phD: “Psst, hey, kid. Over here! Just ten moneys, I’ll give you a ride from all the way point A to B. What are points A and B? That’s up to you- but I’m the cheapest. Don’t listen to the others. Seriously, they’ll chat your ear off. Real annoying if you ask me.”

-> "Could you tell me about something?"
	Dr. Boatguy phD: "Mhm? What is it?"
	<<jump MisinformationBoat>>
-> "I just went back in time, I think. I'm reliving the same day."
	Boatguy raises their eyebrows to an almost comical extent. It seems that- whatever they were expecting you to say- that wasn't it.
	Dr. Boatguy phD: "Ohhh, uh-huh? Dude, I was waiting for this day to come, seriously!"
	Their eyes start sparkling with a sudden, unadulterated glee.
	Dr. Boatguy phD: "Is it.. can you do that all the time? Like.. Go back in time? See the past? The dinosaurs?"
	-> "No.. just back to when I came here."
		Sasha: "No, just when I came here."
		Boatguy beams at you.
	-> "You seem to be enjoying this way too much."
		Sasha: "You seem to be enjoying this way too much."
		You're upset, naturally. You just watched everybody die and here's Boatguy bouncing up and down like you're a creature of legend. 
		They don't stop at your irritation, though.
	Dr. Boatguy phD: "Dude, dude, seriously. You know- I was prepared for this exact moment."
	Dr. Boatguy phD: "Next time you come see me, seriously, tell me my secret word. I have a secret word for this! Then- then I'll be like,"
	They pause for a moment to catch their breath.
	Dr. Boatguy phD: "Your best friend, I think."
	Dr. Boatguy phD: "The secret word is uh, it's Sisyphus."
	What a decadently pretentious word for a man like Boatguy. As an Art major, you can truly appreciate that type of dissipation <<if $ArtMajor == true>>
	Sisyphus? Seriously? <<if $TechMajor == true>>
	Regardless, it would be nice to have someone on your side without having to have this entire conversation again. An oddly helpful thing from the resident nutcase.
	-> "Noted."
		Sasha: "Noted."
	-> "..Sure."
		Sasha: "..Sure."
	They nod vehemently
	<<set $DudeTheyJustSaidThat = true>>
	<<set $SecretWord = true>>
-> "That’s alright."
	<<close>>
-> "Hey, Boatguy.. Sisyphus." <<if $SecretWord == true>> //Knowledge
	<<jump PRANKED>>
-> "Could you take me to the island? " <<if $IslandQuestActive == true>>

